SUMMARY:AYPROS X UNITED WAY: UNITED FOR YOUTH BLOCK PARTY
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Young Professionals (AYPROS)\n*IMPORTANT: YOU MUST R
 EGISTER ON THE HANDS ON WEBSITE TO PARTICIPATE SEE BELOW*\n\nPack Square P
 ark will be filled with young people\, families\, music\, activities\, foo
 d\, and community organizations on Friday\, August 7\, and AYPROS is showi
 ng up to help make it happen.\n\nJoin fellow young professionals as we vol
 unteer with United Way of Asheville and Buncombe County for the 2026 Unite
 d for Youth Community Engagement Block Party. This free\, family-friendly 
 celebration brings together community partners\,\nstudents\, and families 
 before the start of the school year.\n\nThe event supports United for Yout
 h’s Bold Community Goal that every student in Buncombe County will gradu
 ate from high school ready to pursue their goals and dreams.\n\n**AYPROS w
 ill be serving together during the 6:00–8:00 PM volunteer shift.**\n\nDu
 ring our shift\, volunteers will help welcome guests\, distribute food tic
 kets and event information\, maintain water stations\, assist vendors\, ke
 ep shared spaces clean\, and step in wherever additional help is needed.\n
 No previous volunteer experience is required. Come ready to help\, spend t
 ime with fellow young professionals\, and support an evening created for l
 ocal students and their families.\n\n## Register for the AYPROS Volunteer 
 Shift\n\nRegistration must be completed through the Hands On Asheville-Bun
 combe volunteer page.\n\n1. Select the **Friday\, August 7\, 6:00–8:00 P
 M shift**.\n2. Click **Respond** to begin registration.\n3. In the **Respo
 nse Notes** box\, enter:\n\n**I am volunteering with Asheville’s Young P
 rofessionals (AYPROS).**\n**![](https://aypros.wildapricot.org/resources/P
 ictures/FireShot%20Capture%20060%20-%20United%20for%20Youth%20Community%20
 Engagement%20Block%20Party%20-%202026!%20-%20Hands%20O_%20-%20%5Bwww.hands
 onasheville.org%5D.png)**\n\n1. Enter the best phone number for United Way
  to use if there are changes to the volunteer opportunity.\n2. Click **Sig
 n Up for 1 Shift** to complete your registration.\n\nPlease do not arrive 
 unless you have successfully registered for the shift.\n**[\\[REGISTER FOR
  THE AYPROS 6–8 PM SHIFT\\]](https://www.handsonasheville.org/need/detai
 l/?need_id=1269526)**\n\n## The Block Party\n\nThe United for Youth Block 
 Party is an evening celebration featuring live performances\, family activ
 ities\, food\, and representatives from schools\, nonprofit organizations\
 , health providers\, youth programs\, cultural institutions\, and communit
 y agencies throughout Asheville and Buncombe County.\nScheduled performers
  include:\n\n* Asheville Middle Cheer Team\n* School of Rock Academy\n* DJ
  Tennezzee and DJ Oli\n* Beat Yo Feet Go-Go Band Workshop\n* Carolina Diva
  Diamondz\n* CWA Marching Band\n* Solo performances by Max and Autum Maria
 \n* Additional performers and activities throughout the evening\n\nThe blo
 ck party takes place from 5:00–8:00 PM\, so AYPROS volunteers will be se
 rving while the celebration is fully underway.\n\n## AYPROS Volunteer Resp
 onsibilities May Include\n\n* Staffing barricades and restricted-access po
 ints\n* Greeting arriving guests\n* Staffing the ticket booth and distribu
 ting food tickets\n* Handing out maps and event information\n* Helping gue
 sts navigate the event space\n* Distributing water and keeping coolers sto
 cked with water and ice\n* Monitoring water stations\, trash bins\, and wa
 lkways\n* Assisting vendors and helping with dessert service\n* Providing 
 breaks for other volunteers or vendors\n* Serving as a floater and helping
  wherever needed\n* Supporting the overall safety and cleanliness of the e
 vent\n\nFinal assignments will be based on the needs of United Way staff d
 uring the shift.\n\n## What Volunteers Should Know\n\n* Registration throu
 gh Hands On Asheville-Buncombe is required.\n* Select the **6:00–8:00 PM
  shift** so you will be volunteering with AYPROS.\n* Please do not arrive 
 unless you have registered.\n* Arrive at the Volunteer Hub by **5:45 PM**\
 , 15 minutes before the shift begins.\n* Volunteers will sign a waiver at 
 check-in.\n* A volunteer T-shirt will be provided.\n* Food and drinks will
  be available during the event.\n* Wear comfortable\, cool clothing approp
 riate for an outdoor August event with limited shade.\n* Closed-toe tennis
  shoes\, sneakers\, or boots are required.\n* Bring sunscreen and allow ad
 ditional time to park and walk to the Volunteer Hub.\n* Volunteers must be
  comfortable standing on concrete or grass for extended periods.\n* Respon
 sibilities may include bending\, stooping\, walking\, twisting\, and lifti
 ng up to 15 pounds.\n* Volunteers are responsible for their own transporta
 tion to the event.\n* The event is outdoors and will take place rain or sh
 ine.\n\nThe volunteer opportunity is open to ages 12 and older. Youth volu
 nteers must remain with a parent or guardian throughout their shift.\nThe 
 event is listed as wheelchair accessible. Volunteers who require accommoda
 tions should contact the site supervisor through the volunteer registratio
 n page to discuss how they can best be supported.\n\n## Event Details\n\n*
 *Friday\, August 7\, 2026**\n**AYPROS Volunteer Shift**\n6:00 PM–8:00 PM
 \n\n**Volunteer Arrival and Check-In**\n5:45 PM\n\n**Block Party Hours**\n
 5:00 PM–8:00 PM\n\n**Pack Square Park**\n80 Court Plaza\nAsheville\, NC 
 28801\n\n**Cost:** Free\n**Registration:** Required\n**Event Setting:** Ou
 tdoors and rain or shine\n\n## Volunteer Hub and Check-In\n\nThe Volunteer
  Hub will be located on the northwestern side of Pack Square Park near the
  corner of College Street and South Market Street. It is beside the Ashevi
 lle Sister Cities signpost and is outlined in yellow on the map below.\nPl
 ease allow additional time to park and walk to the Volunteer Hub.\n\n![](h
 ttps://aypros.wildapricot.org/resources/Pictures/volunteer-hub.jpg)\n*The 
 Volunteer Hub is outlined in yellow near College Street and South Market S
 treet.*\n\n## About AYPROS Leadership & Service\n\nAt AYPROS\, leadership 
 is not limited to titles. It also means stepping forward\, lending a hand\
 , and doing work that matters.\nThrough Leadership & Service opportunities
 \, young professionals work alongside local organizations addressing real 
 needs across Asheville and Buncombe County. Whether you have volunteered w
 ith AYPROS before or are looking for an easy place to begin\, this is a ch
 ance to give back while getting to know others who care about our communit
 y.
