SUMMARY:AYPROS Government Relations Crew: Real Time Intelligence Center Gu
 ided Tour
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Young Professionals (AYPROS)\n**Transparency in gove
 rnment matters\, especially when it comes to law enforcement.**\n\nJoin th
 e AYPROS Government Relations Crew for a private guided tour of Asheville
 ’s **Real Time Intelligence Center**\, commonly known as the RTIC\, at t
 he Asheville Police Department. This special visit has been arranged speci
 fically for AYPROS in coordination with Interim Police Chief Jackie Stepp 
 and the Asheville Police Department.\n\nThe RTIC has been the subject of c
 onsiderable public discussion. When people do not have access to clear\, f
 irsthand information\, it becomes easier for misinformation\, and sometime
 s deliberate disinformation\, to shape the conversation.\n\nKnowledge is p
 ower. This tour gives AYPROS members the opportunity to ask their question
 s directly to the people responsible for the center and learn how it opera
 tes from the source.\n\nNo secondhand explanations. No social media interp
 retations. No predetermined opinions. This is an opportunity for direct\, 
 firsthand education about a public institution serving our community.\n\nT
 he goal is not to tell members what to think. It is to give them the infor
 mation\, access\, and opportunity to ask thoughtful questions so they can 
 reach their own informed conclusions.\n\n## What to Expect\n\nDuring the t
 our\, participants will:\n\n* Receive a guided look inside Asheville’s R
 eal Time Intelligence Center\n* Learn about the center’s purpose and rol
 e within the Asheville Police Department\n* Hear how technology\, data\, a
 nd information are used to support emergency response and public safety\n*
  Ask questions directly of Asheville Police Department personnel\n* Gain a
  firsthand understanding of an operation that many residents have heard ab
 out but few have seen\n* Explore the importance of transparency\, accounta
 bility\, and public understanding in law enforcement\n\nThis is the kind o
 f informed civic participation the Government Relations Crew was created t
 o encourage: showing up\, listening carefully\, asking responsible questio
 ns\, and learning how local government works beyond headlines and assumpti
 ons.\n\n## Who Should Attend\n\nThis tour is open to AYPROS members intere
 sted in local government\, law enforcement\, public policy\, technology\, 
 privacy\, emergency management\, public safety\, or civic leadership.\nNo 
 prior experience is required. Returning Government Relations Crew members 
 and first-time attendees are equally welcome.\n\n## Event Details\n\n**Wed
 nesday\, August 12\, 2026**\n**9:00 AM - 11:00 AM**\n\nAsheville Police De
 partment\n100 Court Plaza\nAsheville\, NC 28801\n\nPlease allow additional
  time to park downtown and arrive for check-in. Final entrance\, parking\,
  and arrival instructions will be shared with registered attendees before 
 the tour.\n\n## Registration Is Required\n\nThe Asheville Police Departmen
 t must prepare for the number of people attending\, so advance registratio
 n is required. Space is limited\, and members should register only if they
  intend to participate.\nCome prepared to listen\, learn\, and ask questio
 ns. Transparency is most meaningful when public institutions open their do
 ors and community members take the time to understand what happens inside 
 them.
