SUMMARY:828 Lead Candidate Meet & Greet
DESCRIPTION:Asheville Young Professionals (AYPROS)\nWho is asking for your
  vote\, and what do they want Asheville and Buncombe County’s young prof
 essionals to remember when they head to the polls?\n\nJoin Asheville’s Y
 oung Professionals for the **828 Lead Candidate Meet & Greet**\, a nonpart
 isan evening designed to give young professionals direct access to the can
 didates seeking to represent our community.\n\nAYPROS has invited **every 
 candidate appearing on the official ballot in Asheville and Buncombe Count
 y** to participate. Each attending candidate will receive the same brief\,
  timed opportunity to answer one question:\n\n**“Why are you running\, a
 nd what is the one thing you want Asheville and Buncombe County’s young 
 professionals to remember about you when they head to the polls?”**\n\nT
 his will not be a traditional debate or political forum. There will be no 
 rebuttals\, surprise questions or extended speeches. Instead\, candidates 
 will have an equal opportunity to introduce themselves\, explain why they 
 are running and share the message they most want young voters to hear.\n\n
 Following the candidate showcase\, the room will open for a relaxed meet a
 nd greet where attendees can speak directly with candidates\, ask their ow
 n questions and learn more about the people who may soon be making decisio
 ns on behalf of our community.\n\nWhether you follow every local race clos
 ely or are still trying to understand who will appear on your ballot\, thi
 s is an opportunity to become a more informed voter without the pressure o
 r formality of a traditional political event.\n\n**Thursday\, August 20**\
 n**5:30–7:30 PM**\n**Location to be announced**\n\nLight snacks and drin
 ks will be provided.\n\nThis event is open to young professionals and comm
 unity members interested in learning more about the candidates and partici
 pating in the local electoral process.\n\n**Nonpartisan Event Notice**\nAs
 heville’s Young Professionals does not endorse candidates or political p
 arties. All candidates appearing on the official ballot in Asheville and B
 uncombe County are being invited to participate. Every participating candi
 date will receive equal time and consideration. Candidate attendance will 
 be updated as campaigns confirm participation.
